        {
            "_id": "h8ggp2SeId3nH6jd",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/FreeAction.webp",
            "name": "Twelvemonth and a Day",
            "sort": 1100000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "free"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "defensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per year and a day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The green knight is reduced to 0 Hit Points by an attack or spell</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The green knight returns to life with full Hit Points, points at the creature responsible for their death, and vanishes, returning to the First World. Exactly a year and a day later, they reappear in the nearest free space to the creature they pointed at. The green knight immediately targets them with the triggering attack or spell as a free action, either immediately or as soon as the target is within range. The attack or spell uses the same attack modifier, save DC, damage, and any other effects as the triggering effect, but the green knight gets a result on their attack roll one degree of success better than they rolled or the target gets a result on their save one degree of success worse than they rolled.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": [
                        "healing",
                        "primal"
                    ]
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "ChghA1ebay226wvS",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/ThreeActions.webp",
            "name": "Courtly Game",
            "sort": 1200000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 3
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per year and a day</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The green knight offers a test to a creature they can see, challenging them to live up to their ideals. The target must attempt a @Check[will|dc:35] save. If they fail, they must choose one of two paths.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Brave, Bold, and Courteous</strong> The target upholds their edicts and anathema at great personal cost. They immediately receive a grievous blow that reduces them to 0 Hit Points and makes them dying 3 but suffer no further effects; the target's initiative position moves directly before the green knight's turn, as usual. If the target and the green knight are both still alive 14 days later, the green knight appears before them and offers a reward.</p></li><li><p><strong>Fallen Knight</strong> The target strays from its path, possibly falling from grace. For the next year and a day, the target must attempt a @Check[flat|dc:5] before using any ability granted by a class, archetype, or other feature that imposes edicts or anathema. On a failure, the ability has no effect. If the target's abilities don't rely on upholding edicts or anathema (or that target has no edicts or anathema), the target instead takes a –1 penalty to Will saves for the duration. In addition, the green knight can communicate telepathically with the creature for the duration, regardless of distance, as long as both are in either the First World or the Universe.</p>\n</li></ul>"
                },
                "frequency": {
                    "max": 1,
                    "per": "P1Y"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": [
                        "curse",
                        "mental",
                        "primal"
                    ]
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "zw77JoVg72sFVGw3",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp",
            "name": "Cry of Challenge",
            "sort": 1300000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The green knight issues a challenge in a booming voice, daring their foes to face them. Each creature in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:30] must attempt a @Check[will|dc:34] save or be @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Fascinated] by the green knight for 1 minute. This fascinated condition doesn't end if the green knight uses hostile actions against the creature or its allies (though it still ends if any other enemy does so).</p>"
